      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check which of these you meant:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max dose.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total.** For example, 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg two or three times daily, within the 2,550 mg/day limit.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
